{"step_index":1559,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:56:57Z","thinking":"**Evaluating graph center's characteristics**\n\nExamined the properties of graph $P_6$ with $W=4$ and $f=(0, 2, 0, 0, 2, 0)$. Determined that vertices in $V_2 = \\{1, 4\\}$ have eccentricity 4, which is greater than $W-1=3$. Identified that only vertices 2 and 3 have eccentricity less than or equal to 3. Since those vertices have $f(v)=0$, deduced the center of the graph does not have $f(c)=2$, thus it must have $f(c)=0$. Now considering the eccentricity of the center itself.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"tail -n 8 /tmp/agyhome.NWyWnj/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/f458c9cf-488d-4cd8-8365-7c4e4b16e3f9/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Viewing conductor transcript tail","toolSummary":"View conductor transcript tail"}}]}
{"step_index":1560,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:57:00Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:57:00+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:57:01+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n<truncated 3 lines>\n{\"step_index\":1558,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:56:48Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Identifying Hypotheses at Line 539**\\n\\nCurrently examining line 539 of `test_skel.lean`. The hypotheses present at this location are: `G : SimpleGraph V`, `hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G`. The third hypothesis, `hrad`, is incomplete, but linked to `GraphCalc.`. Need to determine what `hrad` stands for. It appears `hrad3` is a hypothesis about the graph's radius, created by the `by_cases` statement: `hrad3 : GraphCalc.radius G ≤ 3`. Thus, we know `hrad` refers to this radius comparison.\\n\\n\\n**Exploring Radius and Roman Weight**\\n\\nConsidering whether it's possible to establish the relationship between the graph's radius and the Roman weight. Initial thoughts involve potentially bounding the radius using eccentricity and ball within concepts. The goal becomes finding a vertex *c* where *ballWithin* of *c* equals the *univ* to constrain the eccentricity, which in turn constraints the radius. Specifically trying to show if *u*, the vertex with label 2, fulfills this condition.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"python3 -c \\\\\\\"\\\\nimport itertools\\\\nfrom collections import deque\\\\n\\\\ndef bfs_ecc(adj, n, v):\\\\n    dist = {v: 0}\\\\n    q = deque([v])\\\\n    while q:\\\\n        curr = q.popleft()\\\\n        for nxt in adj[curr]:\\\\n            if nxt not in dist:\\\\n                dist[nxt] = dist[curr] + 1\\\\n                q.append(nxt)\\\\n    if len(dist) < n:\\\\n        return None\\\\n    return max(dist.values())\\\\n\\\\ndef test_all_f(adj, n):\\\\n    for f in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\\\\n        # check if f is Roman dominating\\\\n        valid = True\\\\n        for v in range(n):\\\\n            if f[v] == 0:\\\\n                if not any(f[u] == 2 for u in adj[v]):\\\\n                    valid = False\\\\n                    break\\\\n        if not valid:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        W = sum(f)\\\\n        rad = min(bfs_ecc(adj, n, v) for v in range(n))\\\\n        if rad + 1 > W:\\\\n            print(f'VIOLATION OF CONJECTURE! n={n}, rad={rad}, W={W}, f={f}')\\\\n            return False\\\\n        # check if exists u with f[u]==2 having ecc(u) <= W - 1\\\\n        centers_2 = [v for v in range(n) if f[v] == 2]\\\\n        if centers_2:\\\\n            min_ecc_2 = min(bfs_ecc(adj, n, v) for v in centers_2)\\\\n            # is min_ecc_2 <= W - 1?\\\\n            # print if not\\\\n            pass\\\\n    return True\\\\n\\\\n# Test P_4, P_5, P_6, P_7, P_8\\\\nfor n in range(2, 9):\\\\n    adj = {i: [] for i in range(n)}\\\\n    for i in range(n - 1):\\\\n        adj[i].append(i + 1)\\\\n        adj[i + 1].append(i)\\\\n    assert test_all_f(adj, n)\\\\nprint('All Roman dominating functions on paths up to P_8 satisfy rad + 1 <= W!')\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Check all Roman dominating functions on paths\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check all f on paths\\\"\"}}]}\r\n{\"step_index\":1559,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:56:53Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:56:53+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:56:53+02:00\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nOutput:\\nAll Roman dominating functions on paths up to P_8 satisfy rad + 1 <= W!\\r\\n\\n\"}\r\n{\"step_index\":1560,\"source\":\"SYSTEM\",\"type\":\"SYSTEM_MESSAGE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:56:53Z\",\"content\":\"The follo